    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Coursera is a for-profit public company, traded under the ticker COUR and registered with the SEC under CIK 0001651562. It was founded in 2012 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California. Its site describes it as offering online courses, Professional Certificates, Specializations, and degrees, with programs from Google, Meta, Anthropic, DeepLearning.AI, and Stanford, among others.\n\nThe site positions AI and data skills prominently. It points learners to the Machine Learning Specialization, the Deep Learning Specialization, the AI Essentials Specialization, and the AI Engineer Professional Certificate, and notes that some learners start with beginner-friendly Python or generative AI courses. Coursera Plus is described as an annual subscription giving unlimited access to thousands of courses, Specializations, and Professional Certificates. The company describes its certificates as providing job-ready skills and a verifiable credential, and says its programs are designed with employers and universities for roles in cybersecurity, UX, data analytics, AI, and business.\n\nIts recorded legal exposure sits in California, at a count of 236.",
